# 1. Executive Summary

The application was vulnerable to **Server-Side Template Injection (SSTI)** in the product description template editor, rendered server-side using the **FreeMarker** template engine.

The application implemented a sandbox intended to restrict access to dangerous FreeMarker utility classes (such as `freemarker.template.utility.Execute`). However, this sandbox failed to restrict Java reflection performed through objects already exposed to the template's data model — specifically the `product` object. By chaining standard Java reflection calls (`getClass()`, `getProtectionDomain()`, `getCodeSource()`, `getLocation()`), it was possible to obtain a `java.net.URL` object, pivot to an arbitrary absolute file path via `URI.resolve()`, and read the contents of a sensitive file (`/home/carlos/my_password.txt`) from the underlying filesystem — completely bypassing the sandbox restrictions.

