# 14. Conclusion

The assessment confirmed the presence of a **Server-Side Template Injection** vulnerability with a **sandbox bypass via Java reflection**. Although the application attempted to restrict access to known-dangerous FreeMarker utilities, it failed to account for reflective escapes reachable through any object exposed in the template's data model.

This demonstrates that blacklist-based sandboxing of template engines is fundamentally fragile: as long as any application object is exposed to user-controlled template code, an attacker can pivot through standard Java reflection to reach JDK classes capable of arbitrary file access, representing a significant risk to the confidentiality of the affected system.
